  "notes": "HONEST FAIL of the CI tier, root cause quantified: with the uniform 3% Laplace gate the R=8/12/16 set fails (per-radius sigma deviation 4.689%, fit R^2=0.9961) while the R=12/16/20 set passes (0.822%, R^2=0.999984). R=8 is only two interface widths (W=4 in the SCMP model) and lies below the resolvable radius R >= 3W required for the Laplace law, so the coarse set is outside the model's validity range rather than evidence against it. The two-level span criterion also fails (3.87%) for the same single reason. Next build: gate R=12/16/20 and R=16/20/24, keep R=8/12/16 as a documented non-gated ladder. No threshold was relaxed and no artifact was edited."
